      "When young people stand at the crossroads between a vocational college and a university, my advice is clear: choose the university whenever it is within reach.",
      "Admittedly, vocational colleges have real strengths. They train practical, job-ready skills and often lead to employment faster, which appeals to students eager to earn early. However, I still believe a university offers deeper and more lasting benefits. Firstly, a university builds a broad academic foundation and cultivates critical thinking, abilities that keep paying off as careers evolve. A friend of mine who studied engineering at university was later promoted to a management role precisely because he could analyse problems, not merely operate machines. Moreover, the wider network and long-term earning potential a degree brings usually outweigh the short-term gap in starting salaries.",
